1
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:51,940
[Mystic Nine]
[Adapted from the novel of Kennedy Xu]

2
00:01:52,130 --> 00:01:55,050
[Episode 20]
[This story is purely fictional]

3
00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:04,220
[Artifact Chest]

4
00:02:04,660 --> 00:02:06,820
[Artifact Chest]

5
00:02:10,590 --> 00:02:12,540
Only two lots remain.

6
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:24,980
Our funds are only enough to bid on one chest.

7
00:02:25,190 --> 00:02:26,540
We'll have to get someone else to win one of them.

8
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,170
The first chest must go to a Chinese bidder.

9
00:02:29,910 --> 00:02:31,980
Tian Zuocheng is new money.

10
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:33,380
He made his fortune recently, and he's hot-tempered.

11
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:36,010
What he fears most is being looked down on.

12
00:02:36,470 --> 00:02:38,340
He can't stand being upstaged.

13
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:39,890
All you have to do

14
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:41,170
is pose as an opium merchant from the south.

15
00:02:41,430 --> 00:02:42,660
Act more arrogant than he is.

16
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:44,100
Throw money around even more lavishly.

17
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:46,610
Once he feels his pride has been challenged,

18
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:47,940
he'll lose his temper.

19
00:02:49,030 --> 00:02:49,850
We have to make sure

20
00:02:49,870 --> 00:02:51,410
he wins one of the chests.

21
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:53,660
Once it's transported out of Beiping,

22
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,850
intercept it on the road.

23
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:09,380
Ladies and gentlemen,

24
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:12,170
we've now come to

25
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,980
tonight's grand finale.

26
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:19,130
A pair of artifact chests from the remote mountains of Xiangxi.

27
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:24,890
Legend has it that each chest contains an ascended mummy.

28
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:27,890
Ancient texts say the ascended mummy

29
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,890
is a relic left behind by an immortal of antiquity.

30
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:33,540
Whoever obtains it can avert calamities,

31
00:03:33,590 --> 00:03:34,730
extend their lifespan,

32
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,660
or reverse life and death.

33
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,260
Its mysteries are beyond measure.

34
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:41,410
But legends are only legends.

35
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:42,820
Whether they're real or not is anyone's guess.

36
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:44,940
Their value lies in the eye of the beholder.

37
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:48,450
The opening bid is 50,000 silver coins.

38
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:51,040
We have to get this one.

39
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:51,970
We can't let it slip away.

40
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,940
What do you think of this lot, Miss Huo?

41
00:04:01,870 --> 00:04:03,940
Are you saying the Empire of Japan

42
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:05,660
isn't worthy of owning it?

43
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:08,170
It's an artifact from the Miao and Yao regions of Xiangxi.

44
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:11,410
It has nothing to do with your country's cultural interests.

45
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:12,660
Why bother bidding on it?

46
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,410
It's too niche.

47
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:15,780
You could end up holding the bag.

48
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:18,020
I think it's worth joining the bidding.

49
00:04:18,830 --> 00:04:19,730
Miss Huo,

50
00:04:20,190 --> 00:04:22,020
are you asking me to give it up?

51
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:32,020
Are you hiding something from me?

52
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:38,610
How can I be your adviser if you don't trust me?

53
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:45,540
Bid however you like.

54
00:04:45,630 --> 00:04:46,170
Very well.

55
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:10,660
The bidding begins now.

56
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:11,980
100,000.

57
00:05:14,030 --> 00:05:15,330
Who's that?

58
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:18,810
Raise your paddle.

59
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:24,660
100,000.

60
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,340
Everyone,

61
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:36,930
I know the rules say that anyone who failed to win three lots

62
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:39,100
can't bid in the late session.

63
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:40,900
But allow me to make my case.

64
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:44,540
I'm an opium merchant from Jiangxi.

65
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,540
I've only just arrived in Beiping.

66
00:05:47,190 --> 00:05:50,140
If anyone plans to do opium business in the future, remember my name.

67
00:05:51,070 --> 00:05:52,460
Tonight, I'm using this auction

68
00:05:52,630 --> 00:05:53,810
to introduce myself.

69
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:56,730
That artifact chest is mine.

70
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:58,980
Whoever lends me two of the earlier lots,

71
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:02,020
I'll give them this artifact chest as interest

72
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:04,370
once I win it.

73
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:06,900
Really?

74
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:09,700
I'll lend him one.

75
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:10,490
Me too.

76
00:06:19,510 --> 00:06:20,340
We've got

77
00:06:21,310 --> 00:06:22,340
plenty of money.

78
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:28,250
So I hope the private boxes upstairs

79
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:29,580
won't place a blanket bid.

80
00:06:30,070 --> 00:06:32,580
Please give those of us in the main hall a chance.

81
00:06:38,830 --> 00:06:41,020
Who does this nobody think he is?

82
00:06:42,390 --> 00:06:43,460
150,000.

83
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:47,540
Private Room No. 2 bids 150,000.

84
00:06:51,270 --> 00:06:52,290
170,000.

85
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:55,050
Private Room No. 1 bids 170,000.

86
00:06:58,870 --> 00:06:59,660
200,000.

87
00:06:59,950 --> 00:07:02,460
Table 13 bids 200,000.

88
00:07:04,510 --> 00:07:05,660
250,000.

89
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:09,020
Private Room No. 1 bids 250,000.

90
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:13,240
- What a big spender. - Exactly.

91
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:16,290
260,000.

92
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:18,170
Sir,

93
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,780
you've reached your credit limit.

94
00:07:21,430 --> 00:07:24,250
Will you be using the money in your deposit chest?

95
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:26,220
Shall I have someone bring it over for verification?

96
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:27,840
He even brings his entire fortune.

97
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:29,070
Exactly.

98
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,460
Sir,

99
00:08:07,870 --> 00:08:09,370
if you're unable to provide additional funds,

100
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,410
the highest valid bid remains

101
00:08:11,430 --> 00:08:12,730
Private Room No. 1's 250,000.

102
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:16,340
250,000, going once.

103
00:08:17,190 --> 00:08:18,370
Any higher bids?

104
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,220
250,000, going twice.

105
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:27,730
Miss Huo,

106
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,810
this treasure is beyond the reach of ordinary people.

107
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,660
Only the Empire of Japan

108
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:34,010
deserves it.

109
00:08:41,390 --> 00:08:42,650
250,000...

110
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:43,530
Everyone,

111
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:46,420
we've got two tons of opium

112
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:49,010
that just arrived in Beiping today.

113
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:50,250
It hasn't been sold yet.

114
00:08:51,150 --> 00:08:52,530
Will the Xinyue Restaurant

115
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:55,530
accept opium as collateral?

116
00:08:56,670 --> 00:08:57,250
No.

117
00:08:57,750 --> 00:09:00,060
That's never been our policy.

118
00:09:00,670 --> 00:09:02,730
You should think carefully.

119
00:09:03,150 --> 00:09:04,530
Soon, I'll be supplying all the opium

120
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,490
in Beiping.

121
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,100
One month's profit

122
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:10,250
would be enough to buy this entire restaurant.

123
00:09:11,870 --> 00:09:12,820
Sir,

124
00:09:13,510 --> 00:09:15,650
the Xinyue Restaurant does not accept opium.

125
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:21,730
Everyone,

126
00:09:23,270 --> 00:09:24,530
do you want opium?

127
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:26,610
I'm going all in today.

128
00:09:27,670 --> 00:09:30,100
I've got two tons of top-grade opium as collateral.

129
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,730
If anyone here is willing

130
00:09:32,790 --> 00:09:33,580
to lend me money,

131
00:09:34,870 --> 00:09:37,940
I'll settle it at 100 silver coins per jin.

132
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:40,060
- One hundred?
- But only during this auction.

133
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:42,420
Think it over.

134
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:45,770
Once this chance is gone, it's gone for good.

135
00:09:46,510 --> 00:09:47,580
One hundred silver coins.

136
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:49,890
Even ordinary opium

137
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:51,530
sells for at least 200 silver coins a jin

138
00:09:51,750 --> 00:09:53,060
these days.

139
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,250
Exactly. That's half price.

140
00:09:55,510 --> 00:09:56,370
It's a bargain.

141
00:09:56,630 --> 00:09:58,580
Opium is in short supply in Beiping right now.

142
00:09:58,870 --> 00:10:00,820
At that price, he may as well be giving it away.

143
00:10:01,390 --> 00:10:02,010
Do you want it?

144
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:02,820
Of course.

145
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:03,490
Yeah.

146
00:10:03,490 --> 00:10:04,690
- Who wouldn't? - I want it.

147
00:10:04,870 --> 00:10:06,490
Master, you can't do this.

148
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:07,980
If you sell at that price,

149
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:09,370
every opium dealer in Beiping

150
00:10:09,670 --> 00:10:11,340
will blame us for undercutting the market.

151
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:15,220
Soon there won't be any dealers left.

152
00:10:15,670 --> 00:10:17,010
Once they try my product,

153
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:19,250
they'll never buy from anyone else again.

154
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:21,730
Come on, everyone.

155
00:10:22,750 --> 00:10:25,580
If you want it, bring me your money now.

156
00:10:26,750 --> 00:10:28,180
- I want some! - Me too!

157
00:10:34,030 --> 00:10:36,460
Master, they're making a big scene.

158
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:38,770
Looks like they're trying to build a reputation

159
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:41,850
using this auction.

160
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:44,130
Could they be after our business?

161
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,770
Should we put them in their place?

162
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:52,340
The fortune teller warned me

163
00:10:53,150 --> 00:10:54,820
that my luck is clashing this month.

164
00:10:55,670 --> 00:10:57,770
He told me to stay calm and not act rashly.

165
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:00,100
Let's wait and see.

166
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,220
300,000.

167
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:12,610
Table 13 bids 300,000.

168
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:14,980
My friend from Jiangxi,

169
00:11:15,630 --> 00:11:17,490
you don't look like you're here to buy antiques.

170
00:11:18,630 --> 00:11:20,100
You look like you're here to seize territory.

171
00:11:23,790 --> 00:11:25,250
Times have changed.

172
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:26,730
When it's time to step aside,

173
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:29,730
you should step aside.

174
00:11:30,790 --> 00:11:32,130
You're certainly making a grand entrance.

175
00:11:32,550 --> 00:11:33,220
I'm just wondering

176
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:35,650
if you can really afford to back it up.

177
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,700
After all, you're spending borrowed money.

178
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:38,700
Of course,

179
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,580
these days are hard.

180
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:42,490
Even Beiping's opium dealers

181
00:11:42,670 --> 00:11:45,130
might not be able to scrape together that much money.

182
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,250
I'm nothing like

183
00:11:47,270 --> 00:11:48,340
you Beiping dealers.

184
00:11:48,630 --> 00:11:49,730
You call yourselves

185
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,730
the Opium Emperor,

186
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:52,890
the Opium King,

187
00:11:53,510 --> 00:11:55,610
but your pockets have actually nothing but loose change.

188
00:11:56,790 --> 00:11:58,180
Let me make one thing clear.

189
00:11:58,910 --> 00:12:02,180
Sooner or later, the opium trade in Beiping will belong to me.

190
00:12:04,150 --> 00:12:05,250
From then on,

191
00:12:05,790 --> 00:12:07,060
I'll be calling the shots here.

192
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:10,340
And this artifact chest is mine.

193
00:12:12,390 --> 00:12:13,420
350,000.

194
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:19,650
Private Room No. 2 bids 350,000.

195
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:32,250
380,000.

196
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:34,980
Table 13 bids 380,000.

197
00:12:35,030 --> 00:12:36,010
400,000.

198
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:37,700
430,000.

199
00:12:38,270 --> 00:12:39,250
450,000.

200
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:39,850
Miss Huo.

201
00:12:39,870 --> 00:12:40,730
470,000.

202
00:12:40,790 --> 00:12:42,530
- What should we do? - 500,000.

203
00:12:42,750 --> 00:12:43,850
As matters stand,

204
00:12:44,510 --> 00:12:45,370
it may look

205
00:12:45,550 --> 00:12:46,650
like they're driving up the price.

206
00:12:47,270 --> 00:12:48,130
But in reality,

207
00:12:48,910 --> 00:12:50,180
they're gambling everything they own

208
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,250
to fight for their business and reputation.

209
00:12:53,270 --> 00:12:55,180
This is bound to end in mutual ruin.

210
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:58,060
Well said, Miss Huo.

211
00:13:01,510 --> 00:13:02,580
Stop bidding.

212
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:03,890
No matter who wins

213
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:05,370
this chest,

214
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:07,460
we'll still have another chance.

215
00:13:08,030 --> 00:13:10,340
I'll contact Beiping's underworld immediately

216
00:13:10,510 --> 00:13:12,300
and have them seize the chest.

217
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:13,100
Hurry.

218
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:13,650
Yes, sir.

219
00:13:21,670 --> 00:13:24,460
I bid 600,000.

220
00:13:25,270 --> 00:13:28,060
Private Room No. 2 bids 600,000.

221
00:13:31,630 --> 00:13:33,010
600,000, going once.

222
00:13:34,910 --> 00:13:37,100
600,000, going twice.

223
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:41,300
600,000, going three times.

224
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,490
It goes to the highest bidder.

225
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:49,420
Congratulations, Mr. Tian.

226
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:07,820
Master,

227
00:14:08,510 --> 00:14:10,180
we're almost out of money.

228
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:11,340
That's enough.

229
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:13,850
We've made our name tonight.

230
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:15,300
Tomorrow, my name

231
00:14:15,510 --> 00:14:16,340
will be on the front page

232
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:17,890
of every newspaper in Beiping.

233
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:19,370
The whole city will know who I am.

234
00:14:20,910 --> 00:14:21,370
Go.

235
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:22,770
Pay the bill,

236
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:24,580
collect the chest, and let's leave.

237
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:25,530
Yes, master.

238
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:32,010
Pay everyone back, and we're out.

239
00:14:41,390 --> 00:14:41,940
Jiu.

240
00:14:44,910 --> 00:14:46,060
One more chest left.

241
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:47,250
Hang in there.

242
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:12,890
This is tonight's final lot.

243
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:16,130
Other than the color,

244
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:17,820
it's almost identical to the previous chest.

245
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:19,940
Looks like this one's going to fetch an astronomical price too.

246
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:22,650
Inside this chest

247
00:15:22,810 --> 00:15:24,010
lies an ascended mummy.

248
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:25,730
A treasure rarely seen in this world,

249
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:27,250
a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

250
00:15:28,030 --> 00:15:29,530
If you miss it tonight,

251
00:15:29,670 --> 00:15:31,220
even a fortune beyond measure

252
00:15:31,390 --> 00:15:33,010
may never buy you another chance.

253
00:15:33,750 --> 00:15:36,180
Don't let this final opportunity slip away.

254
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:38,850
The bidding starts now.

255
00:15:47,630 --> 00:15:50,060
I bid 300,000.

256
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:53,770
Private Room No. 1 bids 300,000.

257
00:15:57,480 --> 00:15:58,980
Any higher bids?

258
00:16:02,750 --> 00:16:04,370
300,000, going once.

259
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,700
300,000, going twice.

260
00:16:13,030 --> 00:16:13,940
300,000,

261
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,060
- going three...
- Place the blanket bid.

262
00:16:18,910 --> 00:16:21,490
Private Room No. 5 places a blanket bid.

263
00:16:22,390 --> 00:16:22,940
President,

264
00:16:23,670 --> 00:16:24,700
"Blanket Bidding" at an auction

265
00:16:24,790 --> 00:16:26,130
means covering the entire sale.

266
00:16:26,390 --> 00:16:27,530
No matter how high the bidding goes,

267
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:29,850
the blanket bidder pays the final price.

268
00:16:30,910 --> 00:16:32,460
Liang Bencai is making sure no one else stands a chance.

269
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,180
What is he trying to do?

270
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:38,370
You can't place a blanket bid!

271
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:41,300
Liang Bencai,

272
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:42,980
what gives you the right?

273
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,490
You're spending our money.

274
00:16:45,750 --> 00:16:46,890
How dare you make this decision on your own?

275
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,370
Take it down!

276
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:49,100
Now!

277
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:58,980
President Tottori,

278
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:02,700
the ascended mummy is a relic left by our Chinese ancestors.

279
00:17:03,390 --> 00:17:05,570
I will never allow the Japanese to take it

280
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:06,700
and carry it overseas.

281
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:11,010
I'm placing this blanket bid today, no matter what.

282
00:17:18,750 --> 00:17:20,570
Freeze every account under his name.

283
00:17:21,030 --> 00:17:22,460
Don't let him spend another cent.

284
00:17:22,640 --> 00:17:23,140
Yes, sir.

285
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:25,090
Be my guest.

286
00:17:25,750 --> 00:17:29,180
The funds we used for verification didn't come from your government.

287
00:17:31,030 --> 00:17:34,290
The account verified by the Xinyue Restaurant belongs to a private local bank.

288
00:17:34,510 --> 00:17:36,220
It has no connection to Japan.

289
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:36,980
Punk!

290
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:39,380
Punk!

291
00:17:47,270 --> 00:17:50,980
That Liang Bencai must be an impostor.

292
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:53,860
Count every cent we have.

293
00:17:54,070 --> 00:17:56,010
We must win that artifact chest.

294
00:17:56,110 --> 00:17:56,570
Yes, sir.

295
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,140
Isn't Liang Bencai

296
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:02,180
the chief editor of Yahe Monthly?

297
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:04,700
That magazine is funded by the Japanese.

298
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:07,010
He has been helping the Japanese

299
00:18:07,030 --> 00:18:07,980
with all kinds of shady business.

300
00:18:08,830 --> 00:18:10,420
So why is he suddenly

301
00:18:10,550 --> 00:18:11,530
standing against them today?

302
00:18:12,270 --> 00:18:13,680
- Exactly. - That's right.

303
00:18:13,680 --> 00:18:14,200
Yeah.

304
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:17,460
Yes, Yahe Monthly is funded by the Japanese.

305
00:18:18,030 --> 00:18:19,330
I've never denied that.

306
00:18:20,310 --> 00:18:21,250
But precisely because of that,

307
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:23,140
we've seen how they've used archaeology

308
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:23,900
as an excuse

309
00:18:24,550 --> 00:18:25,530
to ship our cultural relics, ancient books,

310
00:18:25,550 --> 00:18:27,380
and stone inscriptions overseas,

311
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:29,010
cart after cart,

312
00:18:29,790 --> 00:18:30,860
ship after ship,

313
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,940
over those years.

314
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:36,010
The ascended mummy is no ordinary relic.

315
00:18:37,270 --> 00:18:38,220
I will never allow

316
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:40,700
our national treasures to leave Chinese soil.

317
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:43,180
Otherwise, I'd have no face to face my ancestors.

318
00:18:44,350 --> 00:18:47,250
Today, I will win this artifact chest.

319
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,530
- Exactly! - Well said!

320
00:18:49,550 --> 00:18:52,180
- Well said! - Well said!

321
00:18:53,030 --> 00:18:53,530
That's right!

322
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,380
- We can't let the Japanese have it.
- Right!

323
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:56,500
- Chief Editor Liang is right!
- Never let it fall into Japanese hands!

324
00:18:56,550 --> 00:18:56,930
Exactly!

325
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:57,460
Well said!

326
00:18:57,880 --> 00:19:00,380
Private Room No. 5 has placed a blanket bid.

327
00:19:01,310 --> 00:19:03,460
Any higher bids?

328
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:11,770
If there are none,

329
00:19:12,030 --> 00:19:13,900
this artifact chest belongs to Liang...

330
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:15,290
Place the blanket bid!

331
00:19:19,350 --> 00:19:22,010
Private Room No. 1 places a blanket bid.

332
00:19:28,310 --> 00:19:31,090
I'd like to see just how deep your pockets are

333
00:19:31,830 --> 00:19:33,620
to make you so confident.

334
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:47,940
President,

335
00:19:48,550 --> 00:19:50,380
our available funds total one million.

336
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:51,460
Yes.

337
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:12,810
Miss Huo,

338
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:14,730
do you still advise

339
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:16,290
against bidding?

340
00:20:17,270 --> 00:20:19,570
It's your money. Spend it however you like.

341
00:20:20,310 --> 00:20:21,250
Buy

342
00:20:22,070 --> 00:20:23,530
whichever item you want.

343
00:20:24,590 --> 00:20:26,250
Besides, this is the final lot.

344
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:28,900
Once this auction ends,

345
00:20:29,070 --> 00:20:30,290
you'll give me all of my antidote?

346
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:31,250
Of course.

347
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:35,050
What exactly is the ascended mummy for?

348
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:44,900
Xiangu said the Japanese still have another million.

349
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:46,620
We can risk it.

350
00:20:49,510 --> 00:20:51,940
I bid 500,000.

351
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,810
Private Room No. 1 bids 500,000.

352
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,010
Five hundred thousand?

353
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:57,290
How did the price jump that high right away?

354
00:20:57,830 --> 00:20:58,700
800,000.

355
00:20:58,790 --> 00:21:00,530
Private Room No. 5 bids 800,000.

356
00:21:00,790 --> 00:21:01,730
830,000.

357
00:21:01,790 --> 00:21:03,700
Private Room No. 1 bids 830,000.

358
00:21:03,830 --> 00:21:04,900
One million.

359
00:21:05,110 --> 00:21:07,330
Private Room No. 5 bids one million.

360
00:21:08,790 --> 00:21:09,420
President,

361
00:21:09,830 --> 00:21:11,140
we're almost at our limit.

362
00:21:11,550 --> 00:21:12,860
Requesting more funds from the Empire will take time.

363
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:14,090
1.05 million.

364
00:21:14,750 --> 00:21:17,620
Private Room No. 1 bids 1.05 million.

365
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:19,620
President.

366
00:21:21,830 --> 00:21:23,290
I have personal funds.

367
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:24,380
It's enough to keep us going.

368
00:21:25,110 --> 00:21:25,660
Continue.

369
00:21:26,030 --> 00:21:26,570
Yes, sir.

370
00:21:30,070 --> 00:21:31,180
1.1 million.

371
00:21:31,310 --> 00:21:32,180
1.2 million.

372
00:21:32,270 --> 00:21:33,050
1.3 million.

373
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:34,420
1.35 million.

374
00:21:34,510 --> 00:21:35,420
1.4 million.

375
00:21:35,750 --> 00:21:37,220
I'm sorry, Chief Editor Liang.

376
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:39,660
You've reached the limit of your guaranteed funds.

377
00:21:40,110 --> 00:21:41,570
If you wish to continue bidding,

378
00:21:41,720 --> 00:21:43,330
you'll need to provide additional funds.

379
00:21:43,750 --> 00:21:45,980
Otherwise, you'll be forced to withdraw.

380
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:57,770
Think of something.

381
00:22:00,310 --> 00:22:01,770
Mr. Liang, I've got 50,000.

382
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:02,540
I'll lend it to you.

383
00:22:02,540 --> 00:22:03,380
I've got 30,000.

384
00:22:03,510 --> 00:22:04,420
I've got 70,000.

385
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,330
Me too.

386
00:22:05,350 --> 00:22:06,380
- I've got 50,000. - I've got 80,000.

387
00:22:06,830 --> 00:22:07,730
- I have money too.
- I'll lend you mine.

388
00:22:07,790 --> 00:22:08,570
We'll all lend you money.

389
00:22:08,590 --> 00:22:10,050
- Me too. - We'll all help.

390
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:12,330
- We'll all lend you money.
- We'll all help.

391
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:15,250
An auction has its rules.

392
00:22:15,880 --> 00:22:18,730
If people openly borrow money to keep bidding,

393
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:20,460
they'll be breaking those rules.

394
00:22:21,270 --> 00:22:23,980
If that happens, we will hold each of you accountable.

395
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:26,330
I suggest you think carefully

396
00:22:27,070 --> 00:22:29,900
about whether you can afford the consequences.

397
00:22:35,830 --> 00:22:36,570
Chief Editor Liang,

398
00:22:37,350 --> 00:22:40,570
do you have any additional funds to continue bidding?

399
00:22:49,110 --> 00:22:50,940
All we have left are the times we won in the early session.

400
00:22:51,480 --> 00:22:52,140
Auctioneer,

401
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:56,140
can those lots from earlier be used as collateral?

402
00:23:00,440 --> 00:23:02,860
Since they were purchased through the Xinyue Restaurant,

403
00:23:03,960 --> 00:23:06,050
their authenticity and value are guaranteed.

404
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:08,810
We can buy them back at the reserve price.

405
00:23:10,110 --> 00:23:10,660
Understood.

406
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:19,250
The original purchase price of all the lots was 180,000.

407
00:23:19,480 --> 00:23:21,660
Based on the reserve price, their current collateral value is 108,000.

408
00:23:22,110 --> 00:23:23,900
The amount has now been credited to Chief Editor Liang's account.

409
00:23:28,880 --> 00:23:31,250
Chief Editor Liang's funds have been confirmed.

410
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:32,860
The bidding may continue.

411
00:23:39,640 --> 00:23:41,050
All of their lots combined

412
00:23:41,750 --> 00:23:43,140
only cost 180,000.

413
00:23:49,270 --> 00:23:52,810
I bid 1.6 million.

414
00:23:53,350 --> 00:23:56,050
Private Room No. 1 bids 1.6 million.

415
00:24:01,070 --> 00:24:01,860
Chief Editor Liang,

416
00:24:02,350 --> 00:24:05,050
would you like to add more funds?

417
00:24:09,680 --> 00:24:11,900
I'll ask one last time, Chief Editor Liang.

418
00:24:12,640 --> 00:24:15,530
Would you like to increase your funds?

419
00:24:24,830 --> 00:24:26,420
I don't like a single one of today's auction items.

420
00:24:26,790 --> 00:24:27,770
Put them all up as collateral

421
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:29,050
under Chief Editor Liang's account.

422
00:24:29,440 --> 00:24:30,090
Yes, Miss.

423
00:24:36,310 --> 00:24:38,700
Credit all the money to Mr. Liang's account.

424
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:43,770
Make way!

425
00:24:43,960 --> 00:24:44,810
One at a time, please.

426
00:24:47,110 --> 00:24:47,900
Excuse me.

427
00:24:49,880 --> 00:24:51,240
- One at a time, please.
- Add this to Chief Editor Liang's account.

428
00:24:51,260 --> 00:24:52,080
- One at a time. - Thank you.

429
00:24:52,110 --> 00:24:52,810
One at a time.

430
00:24:54,070 --> 00:24:54,660
Thank you.

431
00:24:54,750 --> 00:24:56,860
Please credit this to Chief Editor Liang's account.

432
00:24:57,030 --> 00:24:58,380
- 500,000. - This is mine.

433
00:24:59,160 --> 00:24:59,900
Mine is 60,000.

434
00:25:00,240 --> 00:25:00,800
Mine.

435
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:01,730
I've got it all down.

436
00:25:01,730 --> 00:25:05,860
[Beiping Branch of the Military Affairs Commission]

437
00:25:11,440 --> 00:25:12,380
No more waiting.

438
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:13,700
If no one else is bidding,

439
00:25:13,880 --> 00:25:14,730
we can close the sale.

440
00:25:15,510 --> 00:25:16,530
Please wait a moment.

441
00:25:16,750 --> 00:25:19,530
Chief Editor Liang still has several transactions that need to be verified.

442
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:37,900
Just now,

443
00:25:38,310 --> 00:25:40,700
many generous donors

444
00:25:40,880 --> 00:25:42,460
who signed as Chinese and local friends

445
00:25:43,400 --> 00:25:46,050
transferred funds to Chief Editor Liang's account.

446
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:50,140
Chief Editor Liang, your funds are now sufficient.

447
00:25:50,440 --> 00:25:51,900
You may continue bidding.

448
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:57,450
Find out immediately

449
00:25:57,510 --> 00:25:58,770
who transferred money

450
00:25:59,750 --> 00:26:01,170
to Liang Bencai.

451
00:26:01,590 --> 00:26:02,180
President,

452
00:26:02,880 --> 00:26:03,900
we don't have access

453
00:26:03,920 --> 00:26:04,900
to the Xinyue Restaurant's financial records.

454
00:26:05,200 --> 00:26:05,700
I'm afraid...

455
00:26:06,110 --> 00:26:08,380
I bid 1.65 million.

456
00:26:08,880 --> 00:26:10,330
Private Room No. 5

457
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:11,860
bids 1.65 million.

458
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:12,940
1.7 million.

459
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:13,900
1.8 million.

460
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:14,770
1.9 million.

461
00:26:14,960 --> 00:26:15,570
2 million.

462
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:16,530
2.1 million.

463
00:26:16,590 --> 00:26:17,460
2.2 million.

464
00:26:17,590 --> 00:26:18,700
2.3 million.

465
00:26:18,750 --> 00:26:20,660
- 2.45 million. - 2.45 million.

466
00:26:21,400 --> 00:26:25,140
Both parties have bid 2.45 million.

467
00:26:26,400 --> 00:26:27,010
Will either of you

468
00:26:28,070 --> 00:26:30,810
raise the bid further?

469
00:26:33,830 --> 00:26:35,010
We're out of money.

470
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:37,770
I know. Figure something out.

471
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:46,460
I'll offer 200,000.

472
00:26:57,640 --> 00:26:59,570
The Empire of Japan and I

473
00:26:59,960 --> 00:27:01,290
will remember your help.

474
00:27:01,960 --> 00:27:04,460
Don't worry. I'll get you the antidote soon.

475
00:27:04,750 --> 00:27:05,810
You'll recover completely.

476
00:27:06,310 --> 00:27:06,940
Thank you.

477
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:09,860
We need to verify the funds.

478
00:27:10,310 --> 00:27:10,980
I'll take it downstairs.

479
00:27:53,100 --> 00:27:55,340
[200,000 yuan]

480
00:27:55,790 --> 00:27:58,010
[200,000 yuan]
Your check was issued by the Xinyue Restaurant.

481
00:27:58,400 --> 00:27:59,700
It can be cashed directly.

482
00:28:01,790 --> 00:28:03,660
Private Room No. 1 bids...

483
00:28:03,750 --> 00:28:04,290
Wait.

484
00:28:06,880 --> 00:28:09,900
That money is for Private Room No. 5,

485
00:28:10,400 --> 00:28:11,660
Mr. Liang Bencai.

486
00:28:16,160 --> 00:28:16,810
Bravo!

487
00:28:17,830 --> 00:28:19,860
Bravo!

488
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:21,460
Private Room No. 5 bids

489
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:23,860
2.65 million, going once.

490
00:28:23,880 --> 00:28:24,420
Nice!

491
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:26,460
2.65 million, going twice.

492
00:28:26,830 --> 00:28:28,940
2.65 million, going three times.

493
00:28:30,510 --> 00:28:31,290
Sold!

494
00:28:31,920 --> 00:28:35,460
- Excellent! - Bravo!

495
00:28:35,460 --> 00:28:37,620
- That's how it's done! - Great!

496
00:28:41,640 --> 00:28:43,420
The final lot of tonight's auction

497
00:28:43,480 --> 00:28:45,250
goes to Mr. Liang Bencai.

498
00:28:45,350 --> 00:28:46,570
Congratulations, Chief Editor Liang.

499
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:48,700
Wonderful!

500
00:28:49,200 --> 00:28:52,050
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations, Chief Editor Liang!

501
00:28:52,110 --> 00:28:53,180
Congratulations, Chief Editor Liang!

502
00:28:53,200 --> 00:28:53,730
Great!

503
00:28:53,790 --> 00:28:54,460
Congratulations!

504
00:28:55,680 --> 00:28:57,900
Congratulations, Chief Editor Liang!

505
00:28:57,960 --> 00:28:59,770
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations, Chief Editor Liang!

506
00:29:05,960 --> 00:29:07,420
Without our antidote,

507
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:09,730
she won't survive this month.

508
00:29:14,270 --> 00:29:17,490
Allow me to introduce the adviser I invited for this auction.

509
00:29:21,110 --> 00:29:21,810
Chief Editor Liang,

510
00:29:22,790 --> 00:29:23,380
I've heard a great deal about you.

511
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:25,660
He's not Liang Bencai.

512
00:29:28,550 --> 00:29:31,250
He must've known Huo Xiangu all along.

513
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:35,090
Go look into it.

514
00:29:36,350 --> 00:29:38,140
Start with the people around Huo Xiangu.

515
00:29:38,160 --> 00:29:39,470
Check every single one of them.

516
00:29:39,510 --> 00:29:39,980
Yes, sir.

517
00:29:42,270 --> 00:29:43,700
Those people from the magazine

518
00:29:44,440 --> 00:29:46,330
actually conspired with them to deceive us.

519
00:29:48,880 --> 00:29:51,380
Lackeys will always be lackeys.

520
00:29:53,030 --> 00:29:54,050
They can never be truly loyal.

521
00:29:55,790 --> 00:29:57,860
Wipe them all out.

522
00:29:58,440 --> 00:29:59,810
Leave no one behind.

523
00:30:00,110 --> 00:30:00,530
Yes, sir.

524
00:30:02,790 --> 00:30:05,770
Mobilize everyone we can.

525
00:30:06,350 --> 00:30:09,660
No matter what happens tonight, no one is leaving with that chest.

526
00:30:11,030 --> 00:30:14,770
I'll take responsibility for whatever chaos follows.

527
00:30:15,070 --> 00:30:15,530
Yes, sir.

528
00:30:20,640 --> 00:30:21,700
Mr. Tottori,

529
00:30:22,240 --> 00:30:24,860
we've always advocated maintaining friendly relations between our two countries.

530
00:30:25,590 --> 00:30:27,220
Perhaps

531
00:30:27,240 --> 00:30:28,700
there has been some misunderstanding.

532
00:30:28,830 --> 00:30:30,250
Misunderstanding or not,

533
00:30:30,590 --> 00:30:31,900
that's for us to decide.

534
00:30:32,960 --> 00:30:35,330
I demand that you immediately seal off the premises

535
00:30:35,790 --> 00:30:37,140
and detain everyone involved.

536
00:30:43,030 --> 00:30:43,420
Mr. Yin,

537
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:44,730
the Japanese are mobilizing soldiers

538
00:30:44,750 --> 00:30:45,900
from the Military Affairs Commission

539
00:30:46,200 --> 00:30:47,700
to lock down the entire building and interrogate everyone present.

540
00:30:48,350 --> 00:30:48,900
Clear the building.

541
00:30:49,270 --> 00:30:50,530
Escort all the guests out immediately.

542
00:30:50,720 --> 00:30:51,250
No mistakes.

543
00:30:51,440 --> 00:30:51,900
Yes, sir.

544
00:30:52,880 --> 00:30:53,330
Move!

545
00:30:53,350 --> 00:30:53,770
Hurry!

546
00:30:53,830 --> 00:30:55,980
No one leaves!

547
00:30:57,790 --> 00:30:58,900
Who gave you permission to go?

548
00:31:00,140 --> 00:31:00,750
This way!

549
00:31:01,480 --> 00:31:02,040
Keep moving.

550
00:31:02,200 --> 00:31:03,040
The Japanese soldiers are here!

551
00:31:03,040 --> 00:31:03,570
Run!

552
00:31:05,240 --> 00:31:06,250
Darn it!

553
00:31:07,030 --> 00:31:09,090
President, everyone's gone.

554
00:31:10,110 --> 00:31:10,770
Those ear slaves

555
00:31:10,790 --> 00:31:12,640
actually pressed their ears against my door

556
00:31:12,880 --> 00:31:14,660
and secretly let everyone escape.

557
00:31:17,070 --> 00:31:20,460
The Xinyue Restaurant has ruined the Empire's plans.

558
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:22,380
Should we make a move against them?

559
00:31:24,720 --> 00:31:26,980
If the Military Affairs Commission weren't protecting them,

560
00:31:27,480 --> 00:31:29,860
I'd have flattened this place tonight.

561
00:31:35,240 --> 00:31:36,330
Let's head back first.

562
00:31:59,680 --> 00:32:00,140
Master Zhang.

563
00:32:00,480 --> 00:32:00,940
Xinyue.

564
00:32:01,310 --> 00:32:01,940
You're here.

565
00:32:03,830 --> 00:32:05,570
Young Lady, this is as far as we can escort you.

566
00:32:05,880 --> 00:32:07,250
The Xinyue Restaurant is a neutral establishment.

567
00:32:07,510 --> 00:32:09,330
By our rules, we can't interfere with where the goods go next.

568
00:32:10,830 --> 00:32:12,220
The Japanese won't let this go.

569
00:32:12,640 --> 00:32:13,860
I need to go back and deal with the aftermath.

570
00:32:14,550 --> 00:32:15,660
Will you be alright?

571
00:32:16,270 --> 00:32:17,380
Don't worry about me.

572
00:32:18,160 --> 00:32:19,700
The Xinyue Restaurant has stood for over a century.

573
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:21,220
We've weathered every storm imaginable.

574
00:32:22,240 --> 00:32:23,330
We'll handle it.

575
00:32:24,960 --> 00:32:25,700
As for you,

576
00:32:26,920 --> 00:32:28,490
you're taking something that large out of the city.

577
00:32:29,550 --> 00:32:30,770
Whatever you do, don't get caught.

578
00:32:31,400 --> 00:32:31,940
Alright?

579
00:32:35,440 --> 00:32:37,420
Don't worry. I know what I'm doing.

580
00:32:43,750 --> 00:32:44,250
Let's go.

581
00:32:58,070 --> 00:32:59,460
Master Zhang, Xiangu...

582
00:32:59,960 --> 00:33:01,330
She has her reasons she can't tell us.

583
00:33:03,920 --> 00:33:04,530
What's happening?

584
00:33:04,830 --> 00:33:05,530
On the way here,

585
00:33:05,680 --> 00:33:07,290
we saw armed Japanese everywhere.

586
00:33:07,720 --> 00:33:09,490
They've set up roadblocks through several blocks. There's no way out.

587
00:33:11,400 --> 00:33:12,490
Master Zhang, what do we do?

588
00:33:16,030 --> 00:33:16,660
Force our way through.

589
00:33:22,920 --> 00:33:23,700
Split up and look for them.

590
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:24,660
Yes, sir.

591
00:33:26,350 --> 00:33:26,810
Move.

592
00:34:00,830 --> 00:34:01,620
There they are!

593
00:34:01,920 --> 00:34:03,250
Take them and the chest!

594
00:34:03,510 --> 00:34:03,980
Xiaoyu,

595
00:34:04,310 --> 00:34:05,700
take Tiezui and Jiu back.

596
00:34:05,880 --> 00:34:06,730
- Now. - Yes, sir.

597
00:34:07,960 --> 00:34:08,900
Nobody move!

598
00:34:17,590 --> 00:34:18,490
Mr. Liang,

599
00:34:19,360 --> 00:34:20,690
come with us.

600
00:34:42,710 --> 00:34:46,460
Mr. Liang, long time no see.

601
00:34:47,550 --> 00:34:48,610
Please get in.

602
00:34:49,150 --> 00:34:51,010
I'll take you to the train station.

603
00:34:53,880 --> 00:34:55,900
You forgot me already, my friend?

604
00:34:56,710 --> 00:34:57,340
My goodness.

605
00:34:59,630 --> 00:35:01,490
The owner of the Xinyue Restaurant asked me to come.

606
00:35:01,510 --> 00:35:02,490
What are you doing?

607
00:35:04,150 --> 00:35:05,010
Step aside.

608
00:35:05,510 --> 00:35:07,570
We're carrying out official duties.

609
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:12,340
Mr. Liang is an expert

610
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:14,260
invited by the American Chamber of Commerce.

611
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:16,740
I have a travel permit.

612
00:35:16,740 --> 00:35:17,420
[Travel Permit]

613
00:35:20,710 --> 00:35:22,820
He's our guest tonight.

614
00:35:23,280 --> 00:35:24,010
He's not under your jurisdiction.

615
00:35:24,070 --> 00:35:24,490
That's right.

616
00:35:25,150 --> 00:35:26,050
Not your concern.

617
00:35:26,670 --> 00:35:28,490
They're criminals.

618
00:35:30,030 --> 00:35:31,170
They incited anti-Japanese sentiment

619
00:35:31,760 --> 00:35:32,690
and provoked the Empire.

620
00:35:33,840 --> 00:35:36,340
They must stay.

621
00:35:37,110 --> 00:35:38,380
Take a good look.

622
00:35:39,110 --> 00:35:41,900
This is a vehicle from the US Consulate.

623
00:35:44,960 --> 00:35:46,170
If you stop this car and arrest these people,

624
00:35:46,190 --> 00:35:48,380
you'll be interfering in American affairs.

625
00:35:49,510 --> 00:35:51,740
Trying to trigger a diplomatic incident between Japan and the United States?

626
00:35:52,760 --> 00:35:55,490
Or is Japan declaring war on America?

627
00:36:00,670 --> 00:36:02,010
Please get in.

628
00:36:05,440 --> 00:36:06,300
Come with me.

629
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:24,260
Darn it!

630
00:36:25,820 --> 00:36:26,590
[Special Execution Order]

631
00:36:26,590 --> 00:36:27,340
Mr. Tottori,

632
00:36:27,630 --> 00:36:28,690
we've received an order from our superiors

633
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:30,530
to fully cooperate with your operation.

634
00:36:35,880 --> 00:36:37,300
They've all escaped.

635
00:36:37,510 --> 00:36:38,940
What use are you now?

636
00:36:39,960 --> 00:36:41,340
We're only following orders.

637
00:36:41,840 --> 00:36:43,980
Is there anything else you'd like us to do?

638
00:36:46,960 --> 00:36:47,570
Get out.

639
00:36:48,400 --> 00:36:49,170
Out!

640
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:21,610
I knew you'd come back.

641
00:37:22,440 --> 00:37:23,420
Because only I

642
00:37:24,280 --> 00:37:25,380
can cure you.

643
00:37:26,400 --> 00:37:27,210
Give me the antidote.

644
00:37:51,360 --> 00:37:53,530
I hate being lied to.

645
00:37:54,710 --> 00:37:56,490
Especially by someone I care about.

646
00:37:57,400 --> 00:37:59,900
You'll have plenty of time to find out

647
00:38:00,440 --> 00:38:01,780
what happens

648
00:38:02,960 --> 00:38:04,690
to people who deceive me.

649
00:38:08,190 --> 00:38:09,010
Guards.

650
00:38:10,960 --> 00:38:12,260
Take her away.

651
00:38:12,880 --> 00:38:14,130
I'll interrogate her personally.

652
00:38:15,400 --> 00:38:16,050
Wait.

653
00:38:20,670 --> 00:38:22,050
The building has been cleared.

654
00:38:22,960 --> 00:38:24,340
Why are you still here?

655
00:38:32,960 --> 00:38:34,090
You're coming home with me.

656
00:38:35,320 --> 00:38:35,940
Stop.

657
00:38:37,110 --> 00:38:38,130
She's a suspect.

658
00:38:38,630 --> 00:38:40,340
She must be interrogated.

659
00:38:41,400 --> 00:38:42,380
On what charge?

660
00:38:42,590 --> 00:38:43,980
She incited anti-Japanese sentiment

661
00:38:44,920 --> 00:38:46,490
at tonight's auction.

662
00:38:48,070 --> 00:38:49,340
Isn't that enough?

663
00:38:50,070 --> 00:38:51,130
What exactly did she say?

664
00:38:53,320 --> 00:38:54,490
We'll know after we question her.

665
00:38:54,630 --> 00:38:56,050
So you have no charge

666
00:38:56,080 --> 00:38:57,010
and no proof.

667
00:38:59,840 --> 00:39:01,340
She's an employee of the Xinyue Restaurant.

668
00:39:02,110 --> 00:39:03,650
She wasn't part of the auction.

669
00:39:04,000 --> 00:39:05,340
She's outside your jurisdiction.

670
00:39:05,360 --> 00:39:06,610
I have a warrant.

671
00:39:08,840 --> 00:39:11,490
I'm authorized to detain anyone suspicious.

672
00:39:13,440 --> 00:39:14,740
Is the Xinyue Restaurant

673
00:39:15,960 --> 00:39:17,490
trying to shield her?

674
00:39:18,440 --> 00:39:20,210
You can't make baseless accusations like that.

675
00:39:20,920 --> 00:39:21,690
Let me tell you this.

676
00:39:22,550 --> 00:39:24,380
She's not only an employee of the Xinyue Restaurant,

677
00:39:25,440 --> 00:39:27,050
but she's also my goddaughter.

678
00:39:27,760 --> 00:39:29,900
I won't allow anyone

679
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:31,170
to bully her.

680
00:39:31,630 --> 00:39:33,090
Everyone knows

681
00:39:33,630 --> 00:39:34,780
the Xinyue Restaurant

682
00:39:36,070 --> 00:39:38,380
is an officially designated trading house of the Central Government,

683
00:39:38,550 --> 00:39:39,900
under the protection of the Ministry of War.

684
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:43,460
That piece of paper means nothing here.

685
00:39:44,550 --> 00:39:45,050
Stop.

686
00:39:45,150 --> 00:39:45,610
Come.

687
00:39:46,190 --> 00:39:46,650
Let's go home.

688
00:39:47,190 --> 00:39:47,780
Stop!

689
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:50,570
I said stop!

690
00:39:52,070 --> 00:39:52,860
Mr. Tottori,

691
00:39:53,360 --> 00:39:54,530
your warrant

692
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:57,380
does not authorize action against Xinyue Restaurant personnel.

693
00:39:57,670 --> 00:39:59,170
We have no authority to touch her.

694
00:40:00,070 --> 00:40:01,460
You...

695
00:40:03,880 --> 00:40:04,420
President.

696
00:40:06,960 --> 00:40:08,090
Did we get the chest back?

697
00:40:08,510 --> 00:40:10,130
The chest and Liang Bencai

698
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:12,460
were taken away

699
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:13,860
by the people from the American Chamber of Commerce.

700
00:40:14,110 --> 00:40:14,900
Darn it!

701
00:40:15,880 --> 00:40:17,380
How are the Americans involved now?

702
00:40:18,150 --> 00:40:19,860
Who are these people?

703
00:40:20,960 --> 00:40:22,010
What about the other chest?

704
00:40:22,960 --> 00:40:24,130
We still don't know.

705
00:40:24,400 --> 00:40:26,170
But I've given the order.

706
00:40:26,920 --> 00:40:27,940
No matter the cost,

707
00:40:28,190 --> 00:40:28,900
we must seize it.

708
00:40:45,860 --> 00:40:48,340
[Xinyue Restaurant Collection Receipt]

709
00:40:50,840 --> 00:40:52,650
Now everyone in Beiping

710
00:40:53,110 --> 00:40:55,090
knows my name.

711
00:41:30,190 --> 00:41:31,650
If you want to pass through here,

712
00:41:32,190 --> 00:41:33,650
pay your toll.

713
00:41:34,510 --> 00:41:35,980
You little punk.

714
00:41:36,550 --> 00:41:38,260
When I was running guns and cargo,

715
00:41:38,510 --> 00:41:40,090
you were still wetting your pants and playing in the mud.

716
00:41:40,630 --> 00:41:42,460
Men, get him!

717
00:42:26,280 --> 00:42:27,260
Mr. Tian.

718
00:42:28,320 --> 00:42:29,260
Black Bear?

719
00:42:29,960 --> 00:42:30,900
No wonder.

720
00:42:31,400 --> 00:42:32,940
The moment I left the auction,

721
00:42:33,030 --> 00:42:34,300
you'd be waiting to ambush me.

722
00:42:34,840 --> 00:42:36,900
Cripple him!

723
00:42:37,320 --> 00:42:38,380
If he dies, I'll take the blame.

724
00:42:38,480 --> 00:42:39,050
Yes, sir.

725
00:42:54,710 --> 00:42:56,860
Kill them. Take the chest.

726
00:42:57,440 --> 00:42:58,300
The Japanese.

727
00:43:11,710 --> 00:43:12,780
Watch your back.

728
00:43:58,070 --> 00:43:58,900
Are you alright?

729
00:44:00,440 --> 00:44:01,210
Go.

730
00:44:01,630 --> 00:44:02,460
Take the chest.

731
00:44:02,840 --> 00:44:04,210
China's treasures

732
00:44:04,760 --> 00:44:06,260
must never fall into Japanese hands.

733
00:44:07,110 --> 00:44:07,820
Don't worry.

734
00:44:08,920 --> 00:44:10,820
Bring it on, you punk.

735
00:44:21,280 --> 00:44:22,650
Boss, we can't beat them.

736
00:44:22,760 --> 00:44:23,420
We should run.

737
00:44:24,630 --> 00:44:25,340
Run?

738
00:44:25,880 --> 00:44:26,780
This is China.

739
00:44:27,190 --> 00:44:28,170
They're the ones who should leave.

740
00:44:28,440 --> 00:44:30,260
Help them get the chest.

741
00:44:30,510 --> 00:44:31,260
Beat the Japanese.

742
00:44:31,480 --> 00:44:32,340
Boss, but...

743
00:44:32,630 --> 00:44:33,380
Now!

744
00:44:33,840 --> 00:44:34,340
Yes, sir.

745
00:45:55,260 --> 00:45:59,420
♪The past fades like smoke♪

746
00:45:59,780 --> 00:46:02,500
♪A choice is made in silence♪

747
00:46:02,780 --> 00:46:05,580
♪In this labyrinthine puzzle♪

748
00:46:05,980 --> 00:46:09,740
♪Who can reach the shore?♪

749
00:46:09,980 --> 00:46:13,420
♪Just an ordinary farewell♪

750
00:46:13,700 --> 00:46:17,100
♪The sun seems to shine bright over our heads♪

751
00:46:17,180 --> 00:46:24,460
♪But this could be our last trip together♪

752
00:46:24,900 --> 00:46:28,180
♪The spring breeze continues outside♪

753
00:46:28,460 --> 00:46:31,700
♪Who was it who left in such haste?♪

754
00:46:31,860 --> 00:46:35,900
♪Caught in the game, the raging waves fall silent♪

755
00:46:36,100 --> 00:46:39,460
♪Who believes in fate?♪

756
00:46:39,700 --> 00:46:43,060
♪For my home and my country, the years pass like a dream♪

757
00:46:43,300 --> 00:46:46,580
♪When the song ends, who will still be waiting?♪

758
00:46:46,900 --> 00:46:50,580
♪With a nod, we bid farewell and set out again♪

759
00:46:50,780 --> 00:46:54,020
♪Take care♪

760
00:46:54,020 --> 00:46:56,580
♪We once raced♪

761
00:46:56,660 --> 00:46:58,580
♪For the dawn♪

762
00:46:58,740 --> 00:47:02,020
♪Ever-lasting bond, a satisfying vindication♪

763
00:47:02,140 --> 00:47:05,420
♪In the web of fate♪

764
00:47:05,420 --> 00:47:08,620
♪No one can escape♪

765
00:47:09,620 --> 00:47:11,460
♪Life and death cut like a blade♪

766
00:47:11,620 --> 00:47:13,180
♪We too were young once♪

767
00:47:13,260 --> 00:47:16,700
♪Fortunate to brave the raging waves together♪

768
00:47:16,900 --> 00:47:19,220
♪Keep the ember lit♪

769
00:47:19,340 --> 00:47:23,860
♪To illuminate the journey ahead♪

770
00:47:23,980 --> 00:47:26,940
♪The spring breeze continues outside♪

771
00:47:27,180 --> 00:47:30,700
♪Who was it who left in such haste?♪

772
00:47:30,820 --> 00:47:34,580
♪Caught in the game, the raging waves fall silent♪

773
00:47:34,900 --> 00:47:38,380
♪Who believes in fate?♪

774
00:47:38,540 --> 00:47:41,540
♪For my home and my country, the years pass like a dream♪

775
00:47:41,780 --> 00:47:45,540
♪When the song ends, who will still be waiting?♪

776
00:47:45,700 --> 00:47:49,420
♪With a nod, we bid farewell and set out again♪

777
00:47:49,540 --> 00:48:00,980
♪Please, do take care of yourself♪
